<section class="api-support" id="support">
  <h2>Support & compatibility</h2>
  <dl>
    <div><dt><span class="api-badge" data-support="stable">Stable</span></dt><dd>Documented compatibility. Breaking changes follow an announced deprecation period.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><span class="api-badge" data-support="preview">Preview</span></dt><dd>Public early access. Breaking changes may occur; review the changelog before upgrading.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><span class="api-badge" data-support="experimental">Experimental</span></dt><dd>Evaluation only. No compatibility guarantee; the endpoint lists its availability requirements.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><span class="api-badge">Internal</span></dt><dd>Platform operation and diagnostics. No external compatibility commitment.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><span class="api-badge" data-support="deprecated">Deprecated</span></dt><dd>Use the linked replacement or migration guide. Removal dates appear only when announced.</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p>Current public APIs are Preview unless marked Experimental. Support labels describe compatibility, not access permissions or a service-level agreement.</p>
</section>
